  The reel_script and slides say the 27-round circumambulation with flowers and tulsi was done at the Perumal temples as a general act, but the article says the 27 circuits were done at the Narasimha/Namagiri Thayar and Ranganathar temples, which is roughly consistent; however, the reel_script says 'நாமக்கல் பகுதியில் மகா விஷ்ணு, மகா லட்சுமியை வழிபட்டனர்' while the article says this worship took place in the Namakkal area generally, so this is acceptable.
  The caption and reel_script state the observance 'நேற்று கார்த்திகை முதல் நாள்' and the time window, which match the article, but the caption's list of four Tamil month first days (வைகாசி, ஆவணி, கார்த்திகை, மாசி) is correct; no factual error found there.
  The slides_spec says 'விரதம் இருந்த பக்தர்கள் பங்கேற்றனர்' as a general statement, while the article says only the devotees at the Ranganathar and Narasimha temples observed the fast and 27-circuit worship; the phrasing overgeneralizes the detail.
